Strong-component H is multiplicative after condensation.  Exact-period
packet capacity phi is multiplicative under CRT, but the LRC safe band is
archimedean and creates a defect.  That defect is the LRC analogue of the
strong-ear insertion profile: keep it as data before forming a scalar.

============================================================================================
S102 CONCLUSION
============================================================================================
1. HYP-2865's no-fixed-cap theorem is visible at packet level: divisor
   loading kills any prescribed finite denominator basis.
2. The productive replacement is a scaled exact-period atlas.  Unit packets
   keep Euler phi multiplicity, mod-7 residue, chi_7, and affine-pair data
   until after the LRC witness predicate is evaluated.
3. The HYP-2883 signed-current graph should be lifted to these packet
   atlases: first prove local conservation on exact-period residue fibers,
   then handle CRT multiplicativity defects as strong-component atoms.
